#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=10 nAlgorithms=6;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree (version 1.0.0-SNAPSHOT) - License GPL v3';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1793974117716'; [Fri Nov 06 15:08:37 CET 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[!Ceratitis capitata sigmavirus (CCapSV): 19 sequences of 1277 sites with the country of each (Morocco, Crete) as a
trait with coordinates. Longdon et al. (2017), Proc. R. Soc. B 284:20162381; the alignment from the authors' Figshare
deposit, DOI 10.6084/m9.figshare.3409420 (CC BY). RazorHaploNet with the Shave filter.]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using RazorNet (version dev)  (Huson and Bryant 2024 ; DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.).
The original input consisted of 19 taxa and 19 DNA sequences of length 1,278.
The Razor Haplo Net method was used (default options) so as to obtain 30 nodes and 32 edges.
The Shave Filter method was used (default options) so as to obtain 27 nodes and 27 edges.

References:
Huson and Bryant 2024: DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.
]

